  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Here is a comprehensive overview of the hotel brands most commonly considered for hotel and branded residences projects in the **Caribbean and Latin America (CALA)**:\n\n---\n\n## 🏨 Hotel Brands Commonly Considered for Branded Residences in the Caribbean & Latin America\n\n### 1. **Marriott International** (Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, W Residences, Edition)\n\nMarriott International maintains a commanding lead in the region, with more than three times as many projects as its nearest rival.\n \nThe surge in demand for branded residences in the Caribbean and Latin America has not gone unnoticed by Marriott, which has offered residences across 15 locations in 11 markets, with key projects including The Residences at The St. Regis Kanai Resort in Mexico, Nekajui (a Ritz-Carlton Reserve Residence) in Papagayo, Costa Rica, The Residences at The St. Regis Cap Cana Resort in the Dominican Republic, and the W Residences in São Paulo, Brazil.\n \nIn the luxury space, being able to use branded residences as leverage in the development process has been extremely important, according to Hugo Mirabal, Director of Feasibility and Development at Marriott International.\n\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Hilton** (Waldorf Astoria, LXR Hotels & Resorts, Conrad, Curio Collection)\n\nHilton has advanced its branded residences strategy with the debut of Waldorf Astoria Residences Costa Rica and the signing of Waldorf Astoria Residences Guadalajara, the first standalone Waldorf Astoria branded residences in the Caribbean and Latin America.\n \nHilton also signed a new ultra-luxury resort and residences in Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica, offering 170 guest rooms and one- to four-bedroom homes, slated to join the LXR Hotels & Resorts collection in 2029.\n \nThe pipeline also includes the Waldorf Astoria Dellis Cay and AMARIS Grace Bay (LXR Hotels & Resorts) in Turks & Caicos, as well as the Waldorf Astoria San Miguel de Allende and Conrad Los Cabos in Mexico.\n\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Hyatt** (Park Hyatt, Andaz, Alila, Thompson, Destination by Hyatt)\n\nCarlos Crovato, Head of Development, Lifestyle at Hyatt Hotels Corp., noted that \"for mixed-use developments with residential, most of our projects are going to have that component,\" as \"the market is asking for them and owners are very much interested in getting a faster return on their investment.\"\n Key Hyatt residential brands active in the region include Park Hyatt (with projects like Park Hyatt Los Cabos and Residences in Mexico) and Andaz (present at Mayakoba, Mexico).\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Four Seasons**\n\nFour Seasons was among the very first brands to enter the branded residences space in the 1980s.\n \nWhen it comes to hotel-branded residences, Four Seasons claims one of the largest shares of the market, with buyers instantly attracted to the brand they already love.\n Four Seasons has a strong presence in Mexico (Mexico City) and Costa Rica, among other CALA destinations.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Ritz-Carlton / Ritz-Carlton Reserve** *(under Marriott International)*\n\nThe Ritz-Carlton brand entered the branded residences market in the early 2000s, including the development of The Ritz-Carlton Grand Cayman Resort in the Caribbean. Developer Mike Ryan created their first collection of Ritz-Carlton branded residences in the Caribbean, and after successfully selling out all 66 private homes, this product became an integral part of the Ritz-Carlton offering.\n The Ritz-Carlton Reserve brand is also active, with projects like Ritz-Carlton Reserve Turks & Caicos.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Rosewood Hotels & Resorts**\n\nAt Mayakoba in Mexico's Riviera Maya, Rosewood is one of four luxury hotels with private residences, including Rosewood Residences Mayakoba.\n \nRLH Properties also has Rosewood Residences Mandarina under development in Mexico.\n Rosewood is widely recognized globally as a key player in branded residences.\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Fairmont / Accor** (Fairmont, Sofitel, Raffles, Banyan Tree)\n\nAccor (Europe's largest hotel group) is expanding aggressively into residences via Fairmont, Sofitel, Raffles, Orient Express, and Banyan Tree.\n \nFairmont is one of the four luxury brands with private residences at Mayakoba, Mexico, through Fairmont Heritage Place Mayakoba.\n\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Six Senses** *(under IHG)*\n\nIHG operates branded residences through Six Senses, which focuses on wellness-integrated residential communities.\n \nSix Senses is among the world-leading hospitality brands commonly sought for luxury branded residences in the Caribbean and Central America region.\n\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Aman Resorts**\n\nUltra-private and architecturally driven, Aman limits its residential portfolio to under 15 projects globally to preserve exclusivity.\n \nResidences branded by Aman have been popular options for the luxury buyer in the Caribbean and Latin America.\n Amanyara Villas in Turks & Caicos is one notable Caribbean example.\n\n---\n\n### 10. **Mandarin Oriental**\n\nMandarin Oriental followed in the footsteps of early pioneers like Four Seasons and Aman, offering travelers permanent accommodation at iconic destinations with the comforts of home.\n \nBranded residences under Mandarin Oriental benefit from the marketing power, reservation systems, and service standards of this established hotel brand.\n\n\n---\n\n### 11. **One&Only Resorts**\n\nOne&Only Resorts is among the most active brands in the branded residences segment globally.\n \nOne&Only Mandarina, located north of Punta Mita in Mexico, is a key CALA project developed by RLH Properties, Mexico's leading branded real estate developer.\n\n\n---\n\n### 12. **Andaz & Banyan Tree** *(Hyatt and Accor, respectively)*\n\nBoth Andaz and Banyan Tree are part of the prestigious Mayakoba development in Mexico's Riviera Maya, each offering distinct hotel and residential experiences.\n\n\n---\n\n## Key Market Trends\n\nFor the most part, luxury hoteliers in the Caribbean region won't discuss new developments without mentioning residential opportunities in the same breath. Providing branded residences is considered a win-win scenario for owners who can see a faster return on investment with buyers coming in on the rental units.\n \nTop countries by number of branded residence projects (completed and pipeline) in the Americas include Mexico, Brazil, and Costa Rica following the U.S.",
